      "problem": "Find the disjoint union of the sets $\\{ -1, 1, \\sqrt{5} \\}$ and $\\{ v, w \\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the sets are disjoint since\n\n$$\n\\{ -1, 1, \\sqrt{5} \\} \\cap \\{ v, w \\} = \\emptyset.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the disjoint union is simply the union:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{-1,1,\\sqrt{5}\\}⊔\\{v,w\\} & =\\{-1,1,\\sqrt{5}\\}\\cup \\{v,w\\} \\\\  & =\\{-1,1,\\sqrt{5},v,w\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
